A||||8||fierohoho||Delay wiper trouble, Help!||||9||
Z||000000||fierohoho||04-25-2001||05:34 PM||||I just pulled the Fiero out of the barn to get it ready for our club spring kick off (e-mail me if you want the time and place) and the Wisconsin Dells run (e-mail again for info) and I need help with a delay wiper problem that I didn't get to last year. Any help to ease the fix is appreciated.<P>The problem: When I turn the wipers on delay (spinning the turn signal arm) nothing happens until I actually click it to low speed then the wipers go, but, not delayed just regular. High is the same. The washer switch doesn't work either but did for a while when I first got the car. It has cruise control and that works fine. I am not the original owner so it is possible the switch was replaced with the wrong one and it never had delays. <P>Does anyone know how or what to check to see if it is a delay system or a non-delay with the wrong switch? <BR>If it is the wrong switch would it be possible to change something out to make it a delay as long as I have the switch? I did check to make sure the wiper motor had a good ground and that wasn't the proble. Thanks for any help.<P>||||reg||9
Z||000001||Bob Englert||04-25-2001||08:11 PM||||I have had problems with the wiper switch in at least 2 of my Fieros.  I have also had to replace the switch on a 87 Astro van I used to own.<P>The wiper switch is actually inside the steering column behind the steering wheel.  It is available from Advance Auto or PartsAmerica.com as GP Sorensen #DS170, runs about $55.  <P>The turn signal stalk is really just a stick as far as the wipers and turn signal are concerned.  The cruise switch is in the stalk, but otherwise there is nothing to it as all.  <P>On my daughter's 87 coupe, the wiper would only go full speed or nothing and you had to turn the stalk just so to get it to turn off.  Replacing the switch in the column has solved the problem completely.<P>You will need to remove the turn signal stalk, steering wheel, lock plate, ignition key tumbler, and the turn signal switch to get to the wiper switch.  It is not really difficult but very time consuming the first time you do it.  It took me about 5-6 hours the first time.  If your tilt mechanism is loose this would be a good time to tighten and locktite the 2 bolts you can reach with things disassembled to this point.<P>Good Luck...<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||04-25-2001||09:37 PM||||The first thing I would do is check the option codes for Delay Wipers.  Its possible that someone had a steering column problem (these have a tendancy to get loose) and replaced the column from another car.  If thats the case and they got a column with a delay wiper wand, then all you would need to do is install the delay module which is under the dash to the right of the steering column.  Non-delay equipped cars would just have a wire connector mounted there, while delay equipped cars will have the module with wiring plugged into either side.  <P>Im not sure of the option code, maybe someone else can help with that.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000003||ICAL||04-25-2001||10:38 PM||||On my 85 my wipers would only work on fast and the wash worked fine.  What solved the delay problem for me was not in the stalk but the circuit board located within easy reach on the back of the wiper motor in the front compartment.  I just swaped it with a junk yard one and everything works great now.  I can set the delay at any speed.  At first this problem seemed to depend on the weather, hot or cold, then complete failure of the delay function.   ||||reg||1
Z||000004||sombre||04-26-2001||12:05 AM||||   I have one that the wash,low & high work on but no delay....Have been told to replace the delay module(by pontiac techs,and local fiero guru) which is the circuit board in the back of the wiper motor.I've yet to try since I have the whole dash out working on the interior.The only thing under the right side of the colum is the dimmer module.Confirmed this with pontiac they show no # for a delay module have to but the whole motor....<BR>                                 Greg||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||04-26-2001||07:42 AM||||The delay feature on my 85SE is very frustrating.  I can vary the delay time but all of the control is in the first few degrees of rotation of the stalk.  It is almost all or nothing.<P>My 85GT works fine.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierohoho||04-26-2001||02:30 PM||||Thanks for the help, I did try to find the option code but no luck. Maybe someone else knows it? I don't think the wiper motor has the circuit board in it in '84 but I will try to contort myself and look under the dash, If you don't hear from me in a week send help. Hopefully I can figure it out as we've had record rainfall this season. Keep the tips comming, Thanks.||||reg||1
